hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16316","He said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from Rifa'ah al-Juhani, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until when we were at al-Kadid, or he said: at Qudayd, men among us began asking permission to go to their families, and he would permit them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: What is the matter with men, that the side of the tree nearer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more hateful to them than the other side? So we did not see among the people at that but weeping. So a man said: Indeed he who asks your permission after this is a fool. So he praised Allah and said then: I testify before Allah: no servant dies testifying that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, truthfully from his heart, then he remains upright, but he shall be led into Paradise. He said: And my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has promised me to admit of my ummah seventy thousand with no reckoning upon them nor punishment, and indeed I hope that you shall not enter it until you and those righteous of your fathers and your wives and your offspring take dwellings in Paradise. And he said: When half the night has passed, or he said: two thirds of the night, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, descends to the lowest heaven and says: I ask none about My servants besides Me; who is he who seeks My forgiveness that I may forgive him; who is he who calls upon Me that I may answer him; who is he who asks Me that I may give him, until the dawn breaks. He said:"
"16317","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from Rifa'ah ibn 'Arabah al-Juhani, he said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Makkah, and the people began asking his permission, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: And Abu Bakr said: Indeed he who asks your permission after this is a fool in himself. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praised Allah and said good, then said: I testify before Allah, and when he swore he said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is no servant who believes in Allah and the Last Day then remains upright but he shall be led into Paradise. And he mentioned the hadith."
"16318","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, a man of the people of Madinah, narrated to me, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from Rifa'ah ibn 'Arabah al-Juhani, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until when we were at al-Kadid, or he said: at 'Arafah, and he mentioned the hadith."
"16319","He said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hisham, meaning al-Dastuwai, narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, he said: 'Ata ibn Yasar narrated to us, that Rifa'ah al-Juhani narrated to him, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until when we were at al-Kadid, or he said: at Qudayd, men began asking permission to go to their families, and they were permitted. He said: So he praised Allah and extolled Him and said good, and said: I testify before Allah: no servant dies testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, truthfully from his heart, then he remains upright, but he shall be led into Paradise. Then he said: And my Lord has promised me to admit of my ummah seventy thousand without reckoning, and indeed I hope that you shall not enter it until you and those righteous of your wives and your offspring take dwellings in Paradise. And he said: When half the night has passed, or a third of the night, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, descends to the lowest heaven and says: I ask none about My servants besides Me; who is he who seeks My forgiveness that I forgive him; who is he who calls upon Me that I answer him; who is he who asks Me that I give him, until the dawn breaks."
